/// Twenty-five pages of KBC season 17, and the richest batch yet.
///
/// The five banks before this one worked through seasons 9 to 13 and the
/// harvest kept thinning -- barely a third of the last twelve pages
/// survived. That looked like the archive running out. It was not. It was
/// those particular episodes: season 17's pages carry far more plain
/// general knowledge and far less of who had just been appointed to what,
/// so this batch keeps about two questions in three.
///
/// What went out, as always: anything resting on recent learning. A film
/// from last year, a cricketer's current team, a summit held in 2025, a
/// Nobel announced last autumn. Those are good questions for a television
/// audience and the wrong questions for him.
///
/// Six pages were wrong, and are dropped or corrected rather than copied:
///
///   * one asked which creature completes "at a ___ pace" and offered four
///     animals, none of them the snail.
///   * one asked which word comes from a Latin phrase meaning "make alike"
///     and answered Xerox. It is fax, from fac simile, and the question is
///     here with the right answer.
///   * one asked which month is named after the king of the Roman gods and
///     answered January. January is named after Janus, who is not that, so
///     the question is here asking what it should have asked.
///   * one gave two different answers in its Hindi and English halves,
///     twice, on different pages.
///   * one asked which old-and-new city-name pairing was wrong and offered
///     four correct pairings.
///   * one named the wrong airport for an IATA code, and one called a
///     retired Test cricketer the active one.
///
/// Answer positions cycle 0, 1, 2, 3.
